    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nAs i understand it mini.clue currently only acts on listed buffers as no mapings are created in non-listed buffers.\r\n\r\nI would love to use the submode feature especially for the window management functionality (e.g. resize, navigate).\r\nFor example i would like to be able to use those from within neotree- or diffview-buffers.\r\n\r\nWould this be possible to achieve?",
