    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I would love to use the submode feature especially for the window management functionality (e.g. resize, navigate). For example i would like to be able to use those from within neotree- or diffview-buffers.\r\n> \r\n> Would this be possible to achieve?\r\n\r\nYes, this is possible by manually calling `enable_buf_triggers` for target buffers.\r\n\r\nHere is an example of automatically doing this for `help` buffers:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal clue_group = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup('my-miniclue', { clear = true })\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\r\n  pattern = 'help',\r\n  group = clue_group,\r\n  callback = function(data) MiniClue.enable_buf_triggers(data.buf) end,\r\n})\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-09-08T14:10:56Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/471#issuecomment-1711737414",
